# Density-group buses (magistrala) — known-good baseline

Snapshot of behaviour the user confirmed as “coraz lepiej” (2026-08-07), plus inter-group avoidance.

## Keep

- Horizontal bus from the leaf group toward the switch (not a vertical trunk on the group edge).
- Placement: Magistrala = shortest cable first, then stack next leaves above (`untangleGroupTowardExit`). Diagonalny = zip switch-port order onto slot reading order (top→bottom, left→right) to cut crossings.
- Lane stack by travel direction / switch above-below (nearest port owns the band edge toward the switch).
- No rozbiegówka: `SWITCH_PORT_RUNWAY_TILES = 0`, `switchPortApproach` = snapped port world.
- Climb/drop on the port column first — no shared horizontal on `leafExit.y`.
- Inter-group occupancy: later bundles avoid already claimed horizontal Ys (same Y is enough — stacked switches with the same port index share a highway). Prefer upward `busYOffset` / large upward offset on the **bus only**. Never translate whole leaf groups from Magistrala / Diagonalny — in-group leaf swaps (`untangleGroupTowardExit`) stay; group seating is "Ułóż grupy" / "Ułóż grupy (magistrale)".
- `Ułóż grupy (magistrale)`: same hub-and-spoke engine with profile `mode: 'magistrala'` — larger circle/hub gaps, thick bus+spoke corridors, place largest groups first, score seats to minimise spoke crossings. Does not change default "Ułóż grupy".
- Final Magistala pass (`resolveOverlapsWithTargetDiagonal`): shared **exact** approach column or main bus Y → short 45° stub (`TARGET_DIAG_STUB_TILES`). Adjacent port columns stay orthogonal. Never long diagonals — farther freeX uses orthogonal drop + short stub. Do not Y-nudge from failed X fans (destroys lane stack).
- `Prosty z grup`: straight port↔port (`exitStyle: 'simple'`, `simplePaths`) — no bus / corridor math. Only in-group leaf swaps (port order → slot reading order). Empty mid-waypoints.
- `Magistrala z grup`: orthogonal (`exitStyle: 'orthogonal'`).
- `Diagonalny z grup`: horizontal stub + offset, then free-angle diagonal (`exitStyle: 'oneBend'`, `fastPath`). Free-angle segments must **not** be Chebyshev-densified in `getConnectorPathPreview` (that creates zigzags); only ortho / 45° are densified. Within a group, all diagonals share one exit angle (`pickSharedOneBendSlope` → median natural slope). Bus lanes use `ONE_BEND_LANE_PITCH` (>1) so long parallel runs do not visually merge. Travel direction is always the group trunk side — clamp the knee into the trunk-side gap so a close/overlapping target cannot flip cables left↔right or shoot bends past the switch.

## Do not regress to

- Chassis-edge runway stubs / reverse “pik” into ports.
- Drop-bundle / fan-only-at-switch experiments that replaced the magistrala shape.
- Collapsing all lanes onto one Y via TOP clamp.
- Routing each group in isolation without reading prior horizontals.

